# `npm version` prefixes its tag with "v" by default, and Obsidian matches a
# plugin release by a tag equal to the manifest version with no prefix — so
# "v0.2.0" produces a release the updater looks straight past. Emptying the
# prefix here makes the documented `npm version minor` produce the right tag
# instead of relying on whoever runs it remembering to correct it afterwards.
tag-version-prefix=""
